import Holonics.Compression.Landmark.Identity
import HolonicsResearch.Compression.Landmark.ChartDensity
import Mathlib.RingTheory.AlgebraicIndependent.TranscendenceBasis
import Mathlib.RingTheory.Algebraic.MvPolynomial
import Mathlib.RingTheory.Polynomial.UniqueFactorization
import Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Finsupp.LinearCombination
import Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Pi

/-!
# The eliminant certificate: a declared dimension is certified by generators, not trusted

[definition] A configuration `V ⊆ Kˢ` is declared with **generators** `gens`, polynomials that
vanish on it, and a **dimension** `d`. The **eliminant certificate** of `d` asks that every set
`S` of `d + 1` coordinates carry a nonzero generator whose variables lie in `S`
(`EliminantCertificate`). Read on the variable sets alone it is a finite check: every
`(d + 1)`-set of coordinates contains the variable set of some nonzero generator (`CoversSets`),
which `decide` runs on declared coordinates. The **coordinate ring** of `V` is `K[x_σ] ⧸ I(V)`
(`CoordinateRing`), and its coordinates are the images of the `x_i` (`coord`).

Sources: #410's box "The executable dimension and eliminant certificate of
`compression::landmark::identity`, beside `Compression/Landmark/Identity`"; the `[open]` paragraph
of `Holonics/Compression/Landmark/Identity`, its third item ("A curve's dimension certificate by a
nonzero generator in every pair of coordinates"); the retired Rust owner
`holonics::compression::landmark::identity` at commit `2d34b819` (`Construction::supported_within`,
`Component::certify_dimension`, `IdentityAtlas::{new, coverage, check_coverage, chart_span, search,
certify}`, `RationalChart::{pullback, vanishes}`, the `Distinguished` witness, and the tests
`a_false_dimension_is_refused` and `a_space_curve_is_certified_by_its_eliminants`); the record
`2026-09-19_A_CERTIFIED_FACE_MAP_KERNEL_RETURNS_THE_TWO_SIDED_ANGLE_IDENTITIES_AND_A_MISSED_COMPONENT_INVENTS_ONE.md`
in `research/records/`, its paragraph "Retired September 28" (the dimension certificate, the search
and its witness); the point case in `HolonicsResearch/Compression/Landmark/ChartDensity`
(`finite_iff_coordinate_certificates`); the atlas rows `landmark.identity-kernel`,
`landmark.coverage-law` and `landmark.chart-density`.

What is proved.

1. [proved-derived; formal-checked] **The check.** `EliminantCertificate gens d` is decidable
   (`decidableEliminantCertificate`; its `Bool` reading `certifyDimension`,
   `certifyDimension_eq_true_iff`), and it is the support check `CoversSets` on the variable sets
   of the nonzero generators (`eliminantCertificate_iff_coversSets`), which Lean decides by running
   it (`decidableCoversSets`, `checkSupports`, `checkSupports_eq_true_iff`). A generator's variables
   lie in `S` when and only when each of its terms uses only coordinates of `S`, the Rust's
   `supported_within` (`vars_subset_iff_supportedWithin`). The Rust's two cases are corollaries of
   the general definition: a point (`d = 0`) asks a nonzero generator in every single coordinate
   (`eliminantCertificate_zero_iff`), a curve (`d = 1`) one in every pair of coordinates
   (`eliminantCertificate_one_iff`); with `d + 1` coordinates in all, any nonzero generator is a
   certificate (`eliminantCertificate_of_card`).
2. [proved-standard; formal-checked] **Its law: the dimension is at most `d`.** If every generator
   vanishes on `V`, a nonzero generator in the variables `S` is a nonzero polynomial relation among
   the coordinates of `S` in the coordinate ring (`not_algebraicIndepOn_of_mem`). So under the
   certificate every `d + 1` coordinates are algebraically dependent on `V`
   (`coordinates_dependent`), an algebraically independent family of coordinates has at most `d`
   members (`card_le_of_certificate`), and an algebraically independent set of coordinate functions
   has cardinal at most `d` (`mk_le_of_certificate`); none of these needs a domain. When `I(V)` is
   prime the coordinate ring is a domain generated by its coordinates (`adjoin_range_coord`,
   `isAlgebraic_adjoin_coord`), a transcendence basis is chosen among them (Mathlib's
   `exists_isTranscendenceBasis_subset`), every transcendence basis has the cardinal `trdeg`
   (`IsTranscendenceBasis.cardinalMk_eq_trdeg`), and so `trdeg_K (K[x_σ] ⧸ I(V)) ≤ d`
   (`trdeg_le_of_certificate`).
3. [proved-derived; formal-checked] **The certificate is load-bearing.** Over an infinite field the
   plane's only identity is `0` (`identityIdeal_univ`), so no generators that vanish on the plane
   certify it as a curve (`not_eliminantCertificate_univ`, `plane_declared_curve_refused`). The
   `x`-axis chart `t ↦ (t, 0)` lands in the line `y = 0`, which carries its certificate, and
   certifies `y`, which is not an identity of the plane: its image ideal is strictly larger than
   the plane's (`axis_chart_invents_an_identity`). Likewise the line `C = 1` declared a point is
   refused in the coordinate `S` (`line_declared_point_refused`, read through
   `eval_eq_of_vars_subset`), and the constant chart `(1, 0)` would certify `S`
   (`point_chart_invents_an_identity`). **The point case joins `ChartDensity`**: a generator in one
   coordinate is a univariate polynomial there (`exists_univariate_of_vars_subset`), so a
   configuration whose vanishing generators carry the `d = 0` certificate is finite
   (`finite_of_eliminantCertificate_zero`, through `finite_iff_coordinate_certificates`), and a
   finite configuration has such generators (`exists_eliminantCertificate_zero_of_finite`,
   `finite_iff_exists_eliminantCertificate_zero`).
4. [proved-derived; formal-checked] **The search.** For a finite family `f : Fin k → K[x_σ]` the
   face of the combination `Σ c_j f_j` along a chart `χ` is a linear map of `c` (`chartPullback`,
   `chartPullback_apply`), and the combination vanishes along the chart when and only when `c` is
   in its kernel (`mem_ker_chartPullback_iff`). Over a chart family the joint kernel
   (`familyPullback`, `ker_familyPullback`) is the set of `c` whose combination lies in the identity
   ideal of the union of the images (`mem_ker_familyPullback_iff`, `ker_familyPullback_eq`, through
   the owner's `certified_eval_iff`); under coverage it is the set of identities of `V` in the span
   (`ker_familyPullback_eq_identities`). On a polynomial chart over an infinite field the kernel is
   read on the pulled-back polynomial, with nothing sampled (`polynomialPullback`,
   `eval_aeval_polynomial`, `ker_polynomialPullback`).
5. [proved-standard; formal-checked] **The witness count.** For `N ≠ 0` and nonzero denominators
   `D_i` with `deg N + Σ deg D_i < m`, among any `m` distinct parameters one has `N(t) ≠ 0` and
   every `D_i(t) ≠ 0` (`exists_param_nonroot`), since `N ∏ D_i` has at most `deg N + Σ deg D_i`
   roots. Over a field of characteristic zero the Rust's integer parameters `0, 1, −1, 2, −2, …` are
   distinct (`alternatingParameter`, `alternatingParameter_injective`), so one of the first
   `deg N + Σ deg D_i + 1` of them is that witness (`exists_alternatingParameter_nonroot`). On a
   polynomial chart a candidate whose pullback is nonzero is refused at one of the first `deg + 1`
   of them, with a nonzero face (`polynomialChart_distinguished`).
6. [proved-derived; formal-checked] **Witnesses.** The circle `x² + y² − 1` carries the `d = 1`
   certificate (`circle_certificate`), and its coordinate ring has transcendence degree at most one
   (`circle_trdeg_le_one`; its ideal is prime by `ChartDensity.unitCircle_irreducible`). The
   Galilean fibre `C² − 1` in the one coordinate `C` carries the `d = 0` certificate and is finite
   (`galilean_point_certificate`, `galilean_points_finite`). The plane with no generator fails the
   `d = 1` certificate (`plane_no_generator`). On variable sets, by `decide`: the twisted cubic's
   generators `y − x²`, `z − x³` fail at the pair `(y, z)` and pass with `y³ − z²` added, and the
   plane `z = 0` of three coordinates declared a curve fails (`twisted_cubic_supports`,
   `plane_in_space_supports`); the twisted cubic's case is also read on its polynomials, which
   vanish on `t ↦ (t, t², t³)` (`twisted_cubic_certificate`, `vars_pow_sub_pow_subset`).

What is not claimed. The decomposition of `V` into irreducible components and each component's
irreducibility are declared, not computed (primary decomposition); a curve's eliminants are supplied
among its generators, not eliminated from arbitrary generators; charts of two or more parameters
(components of dimension two or more) are not modelled. Gröbner completion, Buchberger's S-pair
criterion and the kernel equality `J = ker(face)` stay owed in #410's identity-atlas box, and
Richardson undecidability and the holonomic search are not attempted. The certificate bounds the
dimension from above only: `trdeg = d`, and the density of a chart of dimension `d` in a component,
are not derived from it (the plane-curve case is `ChartDensity.rationalChart_certifies`). The
rational chart's pullback numerator `N = Σ c_m ∏ N_i^{m_i} D_i^{E_i − m_i}` and the relation
`p ∘ χ = N / ∏ D_i^{E_i}` are not written: item 5 is the root count the Rust's witness rests on,
stated on `N` and the `D_i`, and it is joined to the face on polynomial charts only. The `decide`
witnesses read declared variable sets, not variable sets computed from generators. On Mathlib's
`MvPolynomial`, `EliminantCertificate` is decidable by a structural instance that Lean does not
compile, since `MvPolynomial.vars` is noncomputable; the check that runs is `CoversSets` on the
variable sets.

The computational object is the helical pair interaction read on a configuration: a chart is a
navigator's path, one parameter carried into the configuration's points, and a coordinate is a
receiver's reading of a point. A generator in the coordinates `S` is a lock among them, a relation
the readings in `S` keep wherever the point moves; algebraic independence is free motion. The
certificate says that every `d + 1` readings are locked, so at most `d` move freely, and that bounds
the dimension a chart must fill for its image's identities to be the configuration's own. Of the
winding guide's six general objects this touches the faces and placement (the evaluation face, the
coordinates in which a generator is placed, and the kernel the search reads) and the helix (the
chart's parameter, along which the witness is found among `deg N + Σ deg D_i + 1` places); the
pair, the cell holonomy, the tube and the tower thread stay attached.

No `sorry`, no `axiom`, no `native_decide`.
-/

namespace Holonics.Compression.Landmark.EliminantCertificate

open MvPolynomial Holonics.Compression.Landmark.Identity Holonics.Compression.Landmark.ChartDensity

/-! ## 1. The check -/

section Check

variable {σ : Type*} [Fintype σ]

/-- [definition] **The support check**: every `d + 1` coordinates contain one of the declared
variable sets. -/
def CoversSets (supports : Finset (Finset σ)) (d : ℕ) : Prop :=
  ∀ S ∈ Finset.powersetCard (d + 1) (Finset.univ : Finset σ), ∃ T ∈ supports, T ⊆ S

/-- [definition] The support check is decided by running it. -/
instance decidableCoversSets [DecidableEq σ] (supports : Finset (Finset σ)) (d : ℕ) :
    Decidable (CoversSets supports d) := by
  unfold CoversSets
  infer_instance

/-- [definition] The support check as a `Bool`. -/
def checkSupports [DecidableEq σ] (supports : Finset (Finset σ)) (d : ℕ) : Bool :=
  decide (CoversSets supports d)

/-- [proved-derived; formal-checked] The `Bool` check reads the support check. -/
theorem checkSupports_eq_true_iff [DecidableEq σ] (supports : Finset (Finset σ)) (d : ℕ) :
    checkSupports supports d = true ↔ CoversSets supports d :=
  decide_eq_true_iff

variable {K : Type*} [Field K]

set_option linter.dupNamespace false in
/-- [definition] **The eliminant certificate of the declared dimension `d`**: every `d + 1`
coordinates carry a nonzero generator in those coordinates alone. -/
def EliminantCertificate (gens : Finset (MvPolynomial σ K)) (d : ℕ) : Prop :=
  ∀ S ∈ Finset.powersetCard (d + 1) (Finset.univ : Finset σ), ∃ g ∈ gens, g ≠ 0 ∧ g.vars ⊆ S

/-- [definition] The certificate is decidable from the generators' equality and variable sets. -/
noncomputable instance decidableEliminantCertificate [DecidableEq σ] [DecidableEq K]
    (gens : Finset (MvPolynomial σ K)) (d : ℕ) : Decidable (EliminantCertificate gens d) := by
  unfold EliminantCertificate
  infer_instance

/-- [definition] The eliminant certificate as a `Bool`. -/
noncomputable def certifyDimension [DecidableEq σ] [DecidableEq K] (gens : Finset (MvPolynomial σ K)) (d : ℕ) :
    Bool :=
  decide (EliminantCertificate gens d)

/-- [proved-derived; formal-checked] The `Bool` certificate reads the certificate. -/
theorem certifyDimension_eq_true_iff [DecidableEq σ] [DecidableEq K] (gens : Finset (MvPolynomial σ K))
    (d : ℕ) :
    certifyDimension gens d = true ↔ EliminantCertificate gens d :=
  decide_eq_true_iff

/-- [definition] The variable sets of the nonzero generators. -/
noncomputable def supportsOf [DecidableEq σ] [DecidableEq K] (gens : Finset (MvPolynomial σ K)) :
    Finset (Finset σ) :=
  (gens.filter (· ≠ 0)).image MvPolynomial.vars

/-- [proved-derived; formal-checked] **The certificate is the support check on the variable sets of
the nonzero generators.** -/
theorem eliminantCertificate_iff_coversSets [DecidableEq σ] [DecidableEq K] (gens : Finset (MvPolynomial σ K))
    (d : ℕ) : EliminantCertificate gens d ↔ CoversSets (supportsOf gens) d := by
  simp only [EliminantCertificate, CoversSets, supportsOf, Finset.mem_image, Finset.mem_filter]
  constructor
  · intro h S hS
    obtain ⟨g, hg, hg0, hvars⟩ := h S hS
    exact ⟨g.vars, ⟨g, ⟨hg, hg0⟩, rfl⟩, hvars⟩
  · intro h S hS
    obtain ⟨T, ⟨g, ⟨hg, hg0⟩, rfl⟩, hT⟩ := h S hS
    exact ⟨g, hg, hg0, hT⟩

omit [Fintype σ] in
/-- [proved-standard; formal-checked] A generator's variables lie in `S` when and only when each of
its terms uses only coordinates of `S` (the Rust's `supported_within`). -/
theorem vars_subset_iff_supportedWithin (g : MvPolynomial σ K) (S : Finset σ) :
    g.vars ⊆ S ↔ ∀ m ∈ g.support, m.support ⊆ S := by
  constructor
  · intro h m hm i hi
    exact h ((mem_vars_iff_mem_support i).mpr ⟨m, hm, hi⟩)
  · intro h i hi
    obtain ⟨m, hm, him⟩ := (mem_vars_iff_mem_support i).mp hi
    exact h m hm him

/-- [proved-derived; formal-checked] **A point** (`d = 0`): a nonzero generator in every single
coordinate. -/
theorem eliminantCertificate_zero_iff (gens : Finset (MvPolynomial σ K)) :
    EliminantCertificate gens 0 ↔ ∀ i, ∃ g ∈ gens, g ≠ 0 ∧ g.vars ⊆ {i} := by
  simp only [EliminantCertificate, zero_add, Finset.powersetCard_one, Finset.mem_map,
    Finset.mem_univ, true_and, Function.Embedding.coeFn_mk]
  constructor
  · intro h i
    exact h {i} ⟨i, rfl⟩
  · rintro h S ⟨i, rfl⟩
    exact h i

/-- [proved-derived; formal-checked] **A curve** (`d = 1`): a nonzero generator in every pair of
coordinates. -/
theorem eliminantCertificate_one_iff [DecidableEq σ] (gens : Finset (MvPolynomial σ K)) :
    EliminantCertificate gens 1 ↔ ∀ i j, i ≠ j → ∃ g ∈ gens, g ≠ 0 ∧ g.vars ⊆ {i, j} := by
  simp only [EliminantCertificate, Finset.mem_powersetCard, Finset.subset_univ, true_and]
  constructor
  · intro h i j hij
    exact h {i, j} (Finset.card_pair hij)
  · intro h S hS
    obtain ⟨i, j, hij, rfl⟩ := Finset.card_eq_two.mp hS
    exact h i j hij

/-- [proved-derived; formal-checked] With `d + 1` coordinates in all, any nonzero generator is a
certificate. -/
theorem eliminantCertificate_of_card (gens : Finset (MvPolynomial σ K)) {d : ℕ}
    (hd : d + 1 = Fintype.card σ) : EliminantCertificate gens d ↔ ∃ g ∈ gens, g ≠ 0 := by
  constructor
  · intro h
    obtain ⟨g, hg, hg0, -⟩ := h Finset.univ (by simp [Finset.mem_powersetCard, hd])
    exact ⟨g, hg, hg0⟩
  · rintro ⟨g, hg, hg0⟩ S hS
    have : S = Finset.univ :=
      Finset.eq_univ_of_card S (by rw [(Finset.mem_powersetCard.mp hS).2, hd])
    subst this
    exact ⟨g, hg, hg0, Finset.subset_univ _⟩

end Check

/-! ## 2. The law: the dimension is at most `d` -/

section Dependence

variable {σ K : Type*} [Field K]

/-- [definition] The coordinate ring of a configuration: polynomials modulo its identities. -/
abbrev CoordinateRing (V : Set (σ → K)) := MvPolynomial σ K ⧸ identityIdeal V

/-- [definition] The coordinate `x_i` read on `V`. -/
noncomputable def coord (V : Set (σ → K)) (i : σ) : CoordinateRing V :=
  Ideal.Quotient.mkₐ K (identityIdeal V) (X i)

/-- [proved-standard; formal-checked] Evaluating at the coordinates is the quotient map. -/
theorem aeval_coord (V : Set (σ → K)) :
    aeval (coord V) = Ideal.Quotient.mkₐ K (identityIdeal V) := by
  apply MvPolynomial.algHom_ext
  intro i
  simp [coord]

/-- [proved-standard; formal-checked] **A nonzero identity in the variables `S` is a relation among
the coordinates of `S`**: they are not algebraically independent on `V`. -/
theorem not_algebraicIndepOn_of_mem {V : Set (σ → K)} {S : Set σ} {g : MvPolynomial σ K}
    (hg : g ≠ 0) (hvars : (g.vars : Set σ) ⊆ S) (hmem : g ∈ identityIdeal V) :
    ¬ AlgebraicIndepOn K (coord V) S := by
  intro hind
  obtain ⟨g', hg'⟩ := exists_rename_eq_of_vars_subset_range g ((↑) : S → σ)
    Subtype.val_injective (by rwa [Subtype.range_coe])
  have h0 : aeval (fun i : S => coord V i) g' = 0 := by
    have : aeval (fun i : S => coord V i) g' = aeval (coord V) (rename ((↑) : S → σ) g') := by
      rw [aeval_rename]
      rfl
    rw [this, hg', aeval_coord, Ideal.Quotient.mkₐ_eq_mk, Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem]
    exact hmem
  have := hind.eq_zero_of_aeval_eq_zero g' h0
  subst this
  rw [map_zero] at hg'
  exact hg hg'.symm

/-- [proved-standard; formal-checked] The coordinates generate the coordinate ring. -/
theorem adjoin_range_coord (V : Set (σ → K)) :
    Algebra.adjoin K (Set.range (coord V)) = ⊤ := by
  rw [Algebra.adjoin_range_eq_range_aeval, aeval_coord, AlgHom.range_eq_top]
  exact Ideal.Quotient.mkₐ_surjective K _

/-- [proved-standard; formal-checked] A nontrivial coordinate ring is algebraic over the algebra
its coordinates generate. -/
theorem isAlgebraic_adjoin_coord (V : Set (σ → K)) [Nontrivial (CoordinateRing V)] :
    Algebra.IsAlgebraic (Algebra.adjoin K (Set.range (coord V))) (CoordinateRing V) := by
  constructor
  intro a
  have ha : a ∈ Algebra.adjoin K (Set.range (coord V)) := by
    rw [adjoin_range_coord]
    trivial
  exact isAlgebraic_algebraMap (R := Algebra.adjoin K (Set.range (coord V)))
    (A := CoordinateRing V) ⟨a, ha⟩

variable [Fintype σ]

/-- [proved-standard; formal-checked] **Under the certificate every `d + 1` coordinates are
algebraically dependent on `V`.** -/
theorem coordinates_dependent {V : Set (σ → K)} {gens : Finset (MvPolynomial σ K)} {d : ℕ}
    (hcert : EliminantCertificate gens d) (hgens : ∀ g ∈ gens, g ∈ identityIdeal V) :
    ∀ S ∈ Finset.powersetCard (d + 1) (Finset.univ : Finset σ),
      ¬ AlgebraicIndepOn K (coord V) (S : Set σ) := by
  intro S hS
  obtain ⟨g, hg, hg0, hvars⟩ := hcert S hS
  exact not_algebraicIndepOn_of_mem hg0 (Finset.coe_subset.mpr hvars) (hgens g hg)

/-- [proved-standard; formal-checked] **Under the certificate an algebraically independent family
of coordinates has at most `d` members.** -/
theorem card_le_of_certificate {V : Set (σ → K)} {gens : Finset (MvPolynomial σ K)} {d : ℕ}
    (hcert : EliminantCertificate gens d) (hgens : ∀ g ∈ gens, g ∈ identityIdeal V)
    (T : Finset σ) (hT : AlgebraicIndepOn K (coord V) (T : Set σ)) : T.card ≤ d := by
  by_contra hlt
  push Not at hlt
  obtain ⟨S, hST, hS⟩ := Finset.exists_subset_card_eq (s := T) (n := d + 1) hlt
  exact coordinates_dependent hcert hgens S
    (Finset.mem_powersetCard.mpr ⟨Finset.subset_univ _, hS⟩) (hT.mono (Finset.coe_subset.mpr hST))

/-- [proved-standard; formal-checked] **Under the certificate an algebraically independent set of
coordinate functions has cardinal at most `d`**, with no domain hypothesis. -/
theorem mk_le_of_certificate {V : Set (σ → K)} {gens : Finset (MvPolynomial σ K)} {d : ℕ}
    (hcert : EliminantCertificate gens d) (hgens : ∀ g ∈ gens, g ∈ identityIdeal V)
    (t : Set (CoordinateRing V)) (ht : t ⊆ Set.range (coord V))
    (hind : AlgebraicIndepOn K id t) : Cardinal.mk t ≤ d := by
  classical
  rw [Cardinal.mk_le_iff_forall_finset_subset_card_le]
  intro s hs
  obtain ⟨u, -, hinj, himg⟩ := Finset.exists_subset_injOn_image_eq_of_surjOn
    (f := coord V) Set.univ s (by
      intro a ha
      obtain ⟨i, hi⟩ := ht (hs ha)
      exact ⟨i, Set.mem_univ _, hi⟩)
  have hu : AlgebraicIndepOn K (coord V) (u : Set σ) := by
    rw [AlgebraicIndepOn, algebraicIndependent_image hinj]
    have : coord V '' (u : Set σ) = (s : Set _) := by
      rw [← Finset.coe_image, himg]
    rw [this]
    exact hind.mono hs
  rw [← himg, Finset.card_image_of_injOn hinj]
  exact card_le_of_certificate hcert hgens u hu

/-- [proved-standard; formal-checked] **The dimension is at most `d`**: when `I(V)` is prime, the
transcendence degree of the coordinate ring is at most the certified `d`. -/
theorem trdeg_le_of_certificate {V : Set (σ → K)} [(identityIdeal V).IsPrime]
    {gens : Finset (MvPolynomial σ K)} {d : ℕ}
    (hcert : EliminantCertificate gens d) (hgens : ∀ g ∈ gens, g ∈ identityIdeal V) :
    Algebra.trdeg K (CoordinateRing V) ≤ d := by
  have := isAlgebraic_adjoin_coord V
  have := (faithfulSMul_iff_algebraMap_injective K (CoordinateRing V)).mpr
    (algebraMap K (CoordinateRing V)).injective
  obtain ⟨t, hts, ht⟩ := exists_isTranscendenceBasis_subset (R := K) (Set.range (coord V))
  rw [← ht.cardinalMk_eq_trdeg]
  exact mk_le_of_certificate hcert hgens t hts ht.1

end Dependence

/-! ## 3. The certificate is load-bearing -/

section LoadBearing

variable {σ K : Type*} [Field K]

/-- [proved-standard; formal-checked] Over an infinite field the plane's only identity is `0`. -/
theorem identityIdeal_univ [Infinite K] : identityIdeal (Set.univ : Set (σ → K)) = ⊥ := by
  ext g
  rw [mem_identityIdeal_iff, Ideal.mem_bot]
  constructor
  · intro h
    exact MvPolynomial.funext fun x => by rw [h x (Set.mem_univ x), map_zero]
  · rintro rfl x _
    rw [map_zero]

/-- [proved-derived; formal-checked] **No generators vanishing on the whole space certify a
dimension below it.** -/
theorem not_eliminantCertificate_univ [Infinite K] [Fintype σ] {d : ℕ}
    (hd : d + 1 ≤ Fintype.card σ) (gens : Finset (MvPolynomial σ K))
    (hgens : ∀ g ∈ gens, g ∈ identityIdeal (Set.univ : Set (σ → K))) :
    ¬ EliminantCertificate gens d := by
  intro h
  obtain ⟨S, hS⟩ := (Finset.powersetCard_nonempty (n := d + 1) (s := (Finset.univ : Finset σ))).mpr
    (by rw [Finset.card_univ]; exact hd)
  obtain ⟨g, hg, hg0, -⟩ := h S hS
  have := hgens g hg
  rw [identityIdeal_univ, Ideal.mem_bot] at this
  exact hg0 this

/-- [proved-derived; formal-checked] **The plane declared a curve is refused** for any generators
that vanish on it. -/
theorem plane_declared_curve_refused [Infinite K] (gens : Finset (MvPolynomial (Fin 2) K))
    (hgens : ∀ g ∈ gens, g ∈ identityIdeal (Set.univ : Set (Fin 2 → K))) :
    ¬ EliminantCertificate gens 1 :=
  not_eliminantCertificate_univ (σ := Fin 2) (by simp) gens hgens

/-- [definition] The `x`-axis chart `t ↦ (t, 0)`. -/
def axisChart : Unit → K → Fin 2 → K := fun _ t => ![t, 0]

/-- [counterexample; formal-checked] **A declaration without the certificate invents an
identity.** The `x`-axis chart lands in the line `y = 0`, which carries its `d = 1` certificate, and
certifies `y`; `y` is not an identity of the plane, and the chart's image ideal is strictly larger
than the plane's. -/
theorem axis_chart_invents_an_identity :
    (∀ t, axisChart () t ∈ zeroSet (X 1 : MvPolynomial (Fin 2) K)) ∧
      EliminantCertificate ({X 1} : Finset (MvPolynomial (Fin 2) K)) 1 ∧
      Certified (axisChart (K := K)) (fun x => MvPolynomial.eval x (X 1 : MvPolynomial (Fin 2) K)) ∧
      (X 1 : MvPolynomial (Fin 2) K) ∉ identityIdeal (Set.univ : Set (Fin 2 → K)) ∧
      identityIdeal (Set.univ : Set (Fin 2 → K)) <
        identityIdeal (⋃ i, Set.range (axisChart (K := K) i)) := by
  have hcert : Certified (axisChart (K := K))
      (fun x => MvPolynomial.eval x (X 1 : MvPolynomial (Fin 2) K)) := by
    intro _ t
    simp [axisChart]
  have hnot : (X 1 : MvPolynomial (Fin 2) K) ∉ identityIdeal (Set.univ : Set (Fin 2 → K)) := by
    rw [mem_identityIdeal_iff]
    intro h
    have := h ![0, 1] (Set.mem_univ _)
    simp at this
  refine ⟨fun t => by simp [mem_zeroSet, axisChart], ?_, hcert, hnot, ?_⟩
  · exact (eliminantCertificate_of_card _ (by simp)).mpr ⟨X 1, Finset.mem_singleton_self _,
      X_ne_zero _⟩
  · refine lt_of_le_of_ne (identityIdeal_antitone (Set.subset_univ _)) fun h => hnot ?_
    rw [h, ← certified_eval_iff]
    exact hcert

/-- [proved-standard; formal-checked] A polynomial reads only its variables: two points that agree
on them give one face. -/
theorem eval_eq_of_vars_subset {g : MvPolynomial σ K} {x y : σ → K}
    (h : ∀ i ∈ g.vars, x i = y i) : MvPolynomial.eval x g = MvPolynomial.eval y g :=
  hom_congr_vars (by ext; simp) (fun i hi _ => by simpa using h i hi) rfl

/-- [counterexample; formal-checked] **The line `C = 1` declared a point is refused** at the
coordinate `S`: its generator `C − 1` is not in `S` alone. -/
theorem line_declared_point_refused :
    ¬ EliminantCertificate ({X 0 - 1} : Finset (MvPolynomial (Fin 2) ℚ)) 0 := by
  rw [eliminantCertificate_zero_iff]
  intro h
  obtain ⟨g, hg, -, hvars⟩ := h 1
  rw [Finset.mem_singleton] at hg
  subst hg
  have := eval_eq_of_vars_subset (g := (X 0 - 1 : MvPolynomial (Fin 2) ℚ)) (x := ![0, 0])
    (y := ![1, 0]) fun i hi => by
      have := Finset.mem_singleton.mp (hvars hi)
      subst this
      rfl
  simp at this

/-- [definition] The constant chart at `(1, 0)`. -/
def pointChart : Unit → Unit → Fin 2 → ℚ := fun _ _ => ![1, 0]

/-- [counterexample; formal-checked] **A point chart on the line `C = 1` invents `S`**: it lands in
the line and certifies `S`, which is not an identity of the line. -/
theorem point_chart_invents_an_identity :
    (∀ i p, pointChart i p ∈ zeroSet (X 0 - 1 : MvPolynomial (Fin 2) ℚ)) ∧
      Certified pointChart (fun x => MvPolynomial.eval x (X 1 : MvPolynomial (Fin 2) ℚ)) ∧
      (X 1 : MvPolynomial (Fin 2) ℚ) ∉ identityIdeal (zeroSet (X 0 - 1 : MvPolynomial (Fin 2) ℚ)) := by
  refine ⟨fun _ _ => by simp [mem_zeroSet, pointChart], fun _ _ => by simp [pointChart], ?_⟩
  rw [mem_identityIdeal_iff]
  intro h
  have := h ![1, 1] (by simp [mem_zeroSet])
  simp at this

/-- [proved-standard; formal-checked] **A generator in one coordinate is a univariate polynomial
there.** -/
theorem exists_univariate_of_vars_subset {g : MvPolynomial σ K} {i : σ} (hg : g ≠ 0)
    (hvars : g.vars ⊆ {i}) :
    ∃ q : Polynomial K, q ≠ 0 ∧ Polynomial.aeval (X i : MvPolynomial σ K) q = g := by
  obtain ⟨g', hg'⟩ := exists_rename_eq_of_vars_subset_range g (fun _ : Unit => i)
    (Function.injective_of_subsingleton _) (by
      rw [Set.range_const]
      exact_mod_cast hvars)
  have hq : Polynomial.aeval (X i : MvPolynomial σ K)
      (MvPolynomial.aeval (fun _ : Unit => (Polynomial.X : Polynomial K)) g') = g := by
    have hr : (aeval fun _ : Unit => (X i : MvPolynomial σ K)) = rename fun _ : Unit => i := by
      apply MvPolynomial.algHom_ext
      intro u
      simp
    rw [← hg', ← AlgHom.comp_apply, MvPolynomial.comp_aeval]
    simp only [Polynomial.aeval_X]
    rw [hr]
  refine ⟨_, ?_, hq⟩
  intro h0
  rw [h0, map_zero] at hq
  exact hg hq.symm

variable [Fintype σ]

/-- [proved-standard; formal-checked] **The point case joins `ChartDensity`**: generators that
vanish on `V` and carry the `d = 0` certificate make `V` finite. -/
theorem finite_of_eliminantCertificate_zero {V : Set (σ → K)} {gens : Finset (MvPolynomial σ K)}
    (hcert : EliminantCertificate gens 0) (hgens : ∀ g ∈ gens, g ∈ identityIdeal V) : V.Finite := by
  rw [finite_iff_coordinate_certificates]
  intro i
  obtain ⟨g, hg, hg0, hvars⟩ := (eliminantCertificate_zero_iff gens).mp hcert i
  obtain ⟨q, hq, hqg⟩ := exists_univariate_of_vars_subset hg0 hvars
  exact ⟨q, hq, hqg ▸ hgens g hg⟩

/-- [proved-standard; formal-checked] A finite configuration has vanishing generators that carry the
`d = 0` certificate: one univariate polynomial in each coordinate. -/
theorem exists_eliminantCertificate_zero_of_finite {V : Set (σ → K)} (hV : V.Finite) :
    ∃ gens : Finset (MvPolynomial σ K),
      (∀ g ∈ gens, g ∈ identityIdeal V) ∧ EliminantCertificate gens 0 := by
  classical
  choose q hq hmem using coordinate_certificates_of_finite V hV
  refine ⟨Finset.univ.image fun i => Polynomial.aeval (X i) (q i), ?_, ?_⟩
  · intro g hg
    obtain ⟨i, -, rfl⟩ := Finset.mem_image.mp hg
    exact hmem i
  · rw [eliminantCertificate_zero_iff]
    intro i
    refine ⟨Polynomial.aeval (X i) (q i), Finset.mem_image_of_mem _ (Finset.mem_univ i), ?_, ?_⟩
    · exact fun h0 => (MvPolynomial.transcendental_X K i) ⟨q i, hq i, h0⟩
    · have he : Polynomial.aeval (X i : MvPolynomial σ K) (q i) =
          rename (fun _ : Unit => i) (Polynomial.aeval (X () : MvPolynomial Unit K) (q i)) := by
        rw [← Polynomial.aeval_algHom_apply, rename_X]
      rw [he]
      intro j hj
      obtain ⟨u, -, rfl⟩ := Finset.mem_image.mp (vars_rename _ _ hj)
      exact Finset.mem_singleton_self _

/-- [proved-standard; formal-checked] **A configuration is finite when and only when some vanishing
generators carry the `d = 0` certificate.** -/
theorem finite_iff_exists_eliminantCertificate_zero (V : Set (σ → K)) :
    V.Finite ↔ ∃ gens : Finset (MvPolynomial σ K),
      (∀ g ∈ gens, g ∈ identityIdeal V) ∧ EliminantCertificate gens 0 :=
  ⟨exists_eliminantCertificate_zero_of_finite, fun ⟨_, hgens, hcert⟩ =>
    finite_of_eliminantCertificate_zero hcert hgens⟩

end LoadBearing

/-! ## 4. The search -/

section Search

variable {σ K : Type*} [Field K] {k : ℕ}

/-- [definition] **The face of the combination `Σ c_j f_j` along a chart `χ`**, linear in `c`. -/
noncomputable def chartPullback {P : Type*} (f : Fin k → MvPolynomial σ K) (χ : P → σ → K) :
    (Fin k → K) →ₗ[K] (P → K) :=
  (LinearMap.pi fun p => (MvPolynomial.aeval (χ p)).toLinearMap) ∘ₗ Fintype.linearCombination K f

/-- [proved-standard; formal-checked] The pullback map's matrix: `c ↦ (Σ_j c_j f_j(χ p))_p`. -/
theorem chartPullback_apply {P : Type*} (f : Fin k → MvPolynomial σ K) (χ : P → σ → K)
    (c : Fin k → K) (p : P) :
    chartPullback f χ c p = ∑ j, c j * MvPolynomial.eval (χ p) (f j) := by
  simp [chartPullback, Fintype.linearCombination_apply]

/-- [proved-derived; formal-checked] **A combination vanishes along the chart when and only when
its coefficients lie in the kernel.** -/
theorem mem_ker_chartPullback_iff {P : Type*} (f : Fin k → MvPolynomial σ K) (χ : P → σ → K)
    (c : Fin k → K) :
    c ∈ LinearMap.ker (chartPullback f χ) ↔
      ∀ p, MvPolynomial.eval (χ p) (∑ j, c j • f j) = 0 := by
  rw [LinearMap.mem_ker, funext_iff]
  simp [chartPullback, Fintype.linearCombination_apply]

/-- [definition] **The joint pullback over a chart family.** -/
noncomputable def familyPullback {ι : Type*} {P : ι → Type*} (f : Fin k → MvPolynomial σ K)
    (χ : ∀ i, P i → σ → K) : (Fin k → K) →ₗ[K] (∀ i, P i → K) :=
  LinearMap.pi fun i => chartPullback f (χ i)

/-- [proved-standard; formal-checked] The joint kernel is the intersection of the charts'
kernels. -/
theorem ker_familyPullback {ι : Type*} {P : ι → Type*} (f : Fin k → MvPolynomial σ K)
    (χ : ∀ i, P i → σ → K) :
    LinearMap.ker (familyPullback f χ) = ⨅ i, LinearMap.ker (chartPullback f (χ i)) :=
  LinearMap.ker_pi _

/-- [proved-derived; formal-checked] **The joint kernel is the identities of the images in the
span**: `c` lies in it when and only when `Σ c_j f_j` lies in the identity ideal of the union of
the images. -/
theorem mem_ker_familyPullback_iff {ι : Type*} {P : ι → Type*} (f : Fin k → MvPolynomial σ K)
    (χ : ∀ i, P i → σ → K) (c : Fin k → K) :
    c ∈ LinearMap.ker (familyPullback f χ) ↔
      ∑ j, c j • f j ∈ identityIdeal (⋃ i, Set.range (χ i)) := by
  rw [← certified_eval_iff, ker_familyPullback, Submodule.mem_iInf]
  simp only [mem_ker_chartPullback_iff]
  rfl

/-- [proved-derived; formal-checked] The joint kernel as a set: the coefficient vectors whose
combination is certified by the family. -/
theorem ker_familyPullback_eq {ι : Type*} {P : ι → Type*} (f : Fin k → MvPolynomial σ K)
    (χ : ∀ i, P i → σ → K) :
    (LinearMap.ker (familyPullback f χ) : Set (Fin k → K)) =
      {c | ∑ j, c j • f j ∈ identityIdeal (⋃ i, Set.range (χ i))} := by
  ext c
  exact mem_ker_familyPullback_iff f χ c

/-- [proved-derived; formal-checked] **Under coverage the search returns the identities of `V` in
the span**: when the images have the identity ideal of `V`, the joint kernel is the set of
coefficient vectors whose combination is an identity of `V`. -/
theorem ker_familyPullback_eq_identities {ι : Type*} {P : ι → Type*} {V : Set (σ → K)}
    (f : Fin k → MvPolynomial σ K) (χ : ∀ i, P i → σ → K)
    (hcov : identityIdeal (⋃ i, Set.range (χ i)) = identityIdeal V) :
    (LinearMap.ker (familyPullback f χ) : Set (Fin k → K)) =
      {c | ∑ j, c j • f j ∈ identityIdeal V} := by
  rw [ker_familyPullback_eq, hcov]

/-- [definition] **The pulled-back polynomial** of the combination along a polynomial chart
`t ↦ (p_i(t))_i`. -/
noncomputable def polynomialPullback (f : Fin k → MvPolynomial σ K) (p : σ → Polynomial K) :
    (Fin k → K) →ₗ[K] Polynomial K :=
  (MvPolynomial.aeval p).toLinearMap ∘ₗ Fintype.linearCombination K f

/-- [proved-standard; formal-checked] The pulled-back polynomial evaluated at `t` is the face at
the chart point. -/
theorem eval_aeval_polynomial (p : σ → Polynomial K) (g : MvPolynomial σ K) (t : K) :
    (MvPolynomial.aeval p g).eval t = MvPolynomial.eval (fun i => (p i).eval t) g := by
  rw [← Polynomial.coe_aeval_eq_eval, ← AlgHom.comp_apply, MvPolynomial.comp_aeval]
  rfl

/-- [proved-standard; formal-checked] **On a polynomial chart over an infinite field the kernel is
read on the pulled-back polynomial**, nothing sampled. -/
theorem ker_polynomialPullback [Infinite K] (f : Fin k → MvPolynomial σ K) (p : σ → Polynomial K) :
    LinearMap.ker (polynomialPullback f p) =
      LinearMap.ker (chartPullback f fun t i => (p i).eval t) := by
  ext c
  rw [mem_ker_chartPullback_iff, LinearMap.mem_ker]
  simp only [polynomialPullback, LinearMap.coe_comp, Function.comp_apply,
    Fintype.linearCombination_apply, AlgHom.toLinearMap_apply]
  constructor
  · intro h t
    rw [← eval_aeval_polynomial, h, Polynomial.eval_zero]
  · intro h
    exact Polynomial.funext fun t => by rw [eval_aeval_polynomial, h t, Polynomial.eval_zero]

end Search

/-! ## 5. The witness count -/

section Witness

variable {K : Type*} [Field K]

/-- [proved-standard; formal-checked] **The witness count**: with `N ≠ 0`, nonzero denominators and
`deg N + Σ deg D_i < |T|`, some parameter of `T` has `N(t) ≠ 0` and every `D_i(t) ≠ 0`. -/
theorem exists_param_nonroot {ι : Type*} [Fintype ι] {N : Polynomial K} {D : ι → Polynomial K}
    (hN : N ≠ 0) (hD : ∀ i, D i ≠ 0) {T : Finset K}
    (hT : N.natDegree + ∑ i, (D i).natDegree < T.card) :
    ∃ t ∈ T, N.eval t ≠ 0 ∧ ∀ i, (D i).eval t ≠ 0 := by
  classical
  set P := N * ∏ i, D i with hP
  have hP0 : P ≠ 0 := mul_ne_zero hN (Finset.prod_ne_zero_iff.mpr fun i _ => hD i)
  have hdeg : P.natDegree ≤ N.natDegree + ∑ i, (D i).natDegree :=
    Polynomial.natDegree_mul_le.trans (Nat.add_le_add_left (Polynomial.natDegree_prod_le _ _) _)
  by_contra hno
  push Not at hno
  have hroots : T ⊆ P.roots.toFinset := by
    intro t ht
    rw [Multiset.mem_toFinset, Polynomial.mem_roots hP0, Polynomial.IsRoot, hP,
      Polynomial.eval_mul, Polynomial.eval_prod]
    by_cases hNt : N.eval t = 0
    · rw [hNt, zero_mul]
    · obtain ⟨i, hi⟩ := hno t ht hNt
      rw [Finset.prod_eq_zero (Finset.mem_univ i) hi, mul_zero]
  have := (Finset.card_le_card hroots).trans
    ((Multiset.toFinset_card_le _).trans (Polynomial.card_roots' P))
  omega

/-- [definition] The Rust's integer parameters `0, 1, −1, 2, −2, …`: the step's half rounded up,
positive at odd steps. -/
def alternatingParameter (step : ℕ) : ℤ :=
  if step % 2 = 1 then ((step + 1) / 2 : ℕ) else -(((step + 1) / 2 : ℕ) : ℤ)

/-- [proved-standard; formal-checked] The Rust's parameters are distinct. -/
theorem alternatingParameter_injective : Function.Injective alternatingParameter := by
  intro a b h
  simp only [alternatingParameter] at h
  split_ifs at h <;> omega

/-- [proved-standard; formal-checked] **The Rust's `Distinguished` witness**: in characteristic
zero one of the first `deg N + Σ deg D_i + 1` integer parameters has `N(t) ≠ 0` and every
`D_i(t) ≠ 0`. -/
theorem exists_alternatingParameter_nonroot [CharZero K] {ι : Type*} [Fintype ι]
    {N : Polynomial K} {D : ι → Polynomial K} (hN : N ≠ 0) (hD : ∀ i, D i ≠ 0) :
    ∃ step ≤ N.natDegree + ∑ i, (D i).natDegree,
      N.eval (alternatingParameter step : K) ≠ 0 ∧
        ∀ i, (D i).eval (alternatingParameter step : K) ≠ 0 := by
  classical
  have hinj : Function.Injective fun s => (alternatingParameter s : K) :=
    Int.cast_injective.comp alternatingParameter_injective
  obtain ⟨t, ht, hNt, hDt⟩ := exists_param_nonroot hN hD
    (T := (Finset.range (N.natDegree + ∑ i, (D i).natDegree + 1)).image
      fun s => (alternatingParameter s : K)) (by
        rw [Finset.card_image_of_injective _ hinj, Finset.card_range]
        omega)
  obtain ⟨step, hstep, rfl⟩ := Finset.mem_image.mp ht
  exact ⟨step, Nat.lt_succ_iff.mp (Finset.mem_range.mp hstep), hNt, hDt⟩

/-- [proved-derived; formal-checked] **A candidate that is no identity on a polynomial chart is
refused at one of the first `deg + 1` integer parameters**, with a nonzero face at the chart point. -/
theorem polynomialChart_distinguished [CharZero K] {σ : Type*} (p : σ → Polynomial K)
    {g : MvPolynomial σ K} (hg : MvPolynomial.aeval p g ≠ 0) :
    ∃ step ≤ (MvPolynomial.aeval p g).natDegree,
      MvPolynomial.eval (fun i => (p i).eval (alternatingParameter step : K)) g ≠ 0 := by
  obtain ⟨step, hstep, hN, -⟩ := exists_alternatingParameter_nonroot (ι := Empty) hg
    (D := fun e => e.elim) (fun e => e.elim)
  refine ⟨step, by simpa using hstep, ?_⟩
  rwa [← eval_aeval_polynomial]

end Witness

/-! ## 6. Witnesses -/

section Witnesses

/-- [proved-derived; formal-checked] **The circle carries the curve's certificate** on its two
coordinates. -/
theorem circle_certificate : EliminantCertificate ({unitCircle} : Finset (MvPolynomial (Fin 2) ℚ)) 1 :=
  (eliminantCertificate_of_card _ (by simp)).mpr
    ⟨unitCircle, Finset.mem_singleton_self _, unitCircle_irreducible.ne_zero⟩

/-- [proved-derived; formal-checked] **The circle's coordinate ring has transcendence degree at most
one**: its identity ideal is `(x² + y² − 1)`, prime, and the certificate bounds the degree. -/
theorem circle_trdeg_le_one : Algebra.trdeg ℚ (CoordinateRing (zeroSet unitCircle)) ≤ 1 := by
  have hI : identityIdeal (zeroSet unitCircle) = Ideal.span {unitCircle} :=
    circleChart_image_ideal.2.1.symm.trans circleChart_image_ideal.1
  have : (identityIdeal (zeroSet unitCircle)).IsPrime := by
    rw [hI, Ideal.span_singleton_prime unitCircle_irreducible.ne_zero]
    exact unitCircle_irreducible.prime
  have := trdeg_le_of_certificate (V := zeroSet unitCircle) circle_certificate (by
    intro g hg
    rw [Finset.mem_singleton] at hg
    subst hg
    rw [mem_identityIdeal_iff]
    exact fun x hx => hx)
  exact_mod_cast this

/-- [definition] The Galilean fibre read in the one coordinate `C`: `C² = 1`. -/
def galileanPoints : Set (Fin 1 → ℚ) := {x | x 0 ^ 2 = 1}

/-- [proved-derived; formal-checked] **The Galilean fibre in one coordinate carries the point's
certificate**: `C² − 1` is a nonzero generator in `C` that vanishes on it. -/
theorem galilean_point_certificate :
    EliminantCertificate ({X 0 ^ 2 - 1} : Finset (MvPolynomial (Fin 1) ℚ)) 0 ∧
      ∀ g ∈ ({X 0 ^ 2 - 1} : Finset (MvPolynomial (Fin 1) ℚ)), g ∈ identityIdeal galileanPoints := by
  refine ⟨(eliminantCertificate_of_card _ (by simp)).mpr ⟨X 0 ^ 2 - 1, Finset.mem_singleton_self _,
    fun h => ?_⟩, ?_⟩
  · have := congrArg (MvPolynomial.eval (0 : Fin 1 → ℚ)) h
    simp at this
  · intro g hg
    rw [Finset.mem_singleton] at hg
    subst hg
    rw [mem_identityIdeal_iff]
    intro x hx
    simp only [galileanPoints, Set.mem_ofPred_eq] at hx
    simp [hx]

/-- [proved-derived; formal-checked] The Galilean fibre in one coordinate is finite, by the point
case's join. -/
theorem galilean_points_finite : galileanPoints.Finite :=
  finite_of_eliminantCertificate_zero galilean_point_certificate.1 galilean_point_certificate.2

/-- [counterexample; formal-checked] **The plane with no generator fails the curve's
certificate.** -/
theorem plane_no_generator :
    ¬ EliminantCertificate (∅ : Finset (MvPolynomial (Fin 2) ℚ)) 1 := by
  rw [eliminantCertificate_of_card _ (by simp)]
  simp

/-- [proved-standard; formal-checked] A binomial `x_a^m − x_b^n` has its variables among `a`, `b`. -/
theorem vars_pow_sub_pow_subset {σ K : Type*} [Field K] [DecidableEq σ] (a b : σ) (m n : ℕ) :
    (X a ^ m - X b ^ n : MvPolynomial σ K).vars ⊆ {a, b} := by
  intro i hi
  rcases Finset.mem_union.mp (vars_sub_subset _ hi) with h | h
  · have := vars_pow _ _ h
    rw [vars_X] at this
    rw [Finset.mem_singleton.mp this]
    exact Finset.mem_insert_self _ _
  · have := vars_pow _ _ h
    rw [vars_X] at this
    rw [Finset.mem_singleton.mp this]
    exact Finset.mem_insert_of_mem (Finset.mem_singleton_self _)

/-- [proved-derived; formal-checked] **The twisted cubic is certified by its eliminants** (the Rust's
test): `y − x²`, `z − x³` and `y³ − z²` vanish on `t ↦ (t, t², t³)`; the first two have no
generator in the pair `(y, z)` and fail the curve's certificate, and with `y³ − z²` added it holds. -/
theorem twisted_cubic_certificate :
    (∀ g ∈ ({X 1 - X 0 ^ 2, X 2 - X 0 ^ 3, X 1 ^ 3 - X 2 ^ 2} : Finset (MvPolynomial (Fin 3) ℚ)),
      ∀ t : ℚ, MvPolynomial.eval ![t, t ^ 2, t ^ 3] g = 0) ∧
    ¬ EliminantCertificate ({X 1 - X 0 ^ 2, X 2 - X 0 ^ 3} : Finset (MvPolynomial (Fin 3) ℚ)) 1 ∧
      EliminantCertificate
        ({X 1 - X 0 ^ 2, X 2 - X 0 ^ 3, X 1 ^ 3 - X 2 ^ 2} : Finset (MvPolynomial (Fin 3) ℚ)) 1 := by
  refine ⟨?_, ?_, ?_⟩
  · intro g hg t
    simp only [Finset.mem_insert, Finset.mem_singleton] at hg
    rcases hg with rfl | rfl | rfl
    · simp
    · simp
    · simp
      ring
  · rw [eliminantCertificate_one_iff]
    intro h
    obtain ⟨g, hg, -, hvars⟩ := h 1 2 (by decide)
    have key := eval_eq_of_vars_subset (g := g) (x := ![0, 0, 0]) (y := ![1, 0, 0]) fun i hi => by
      have := hvars hi
      simp only [Finset.mem_insert, Finset.mem_singleton] at this
      rcases this with rfl | rfl <;> rfl
    simp only [Finset.mem_insert, Finset.mem_singleton] at hg
    rcases hg with rfl | rfl <;> simp at key
  · have h01 : (X 1 - X 0 ^ 2 : MvPolynomial (Fin 3) ℚ) ≠ 0 := fun h => by
      have := congrArg (MvPolynomial.eval ![0, 1, 0]) h
